<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 8.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 8.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport division of BG plc, on Monday announced the following data and forecasts for gas use in the period 6 to 8 April.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 6 (actual) 208 mcm, 49 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 7 (forecast) 225 mcm, 53 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 8 (forecast) 227 mcm, 53 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 6 (actual) 9.2 Celsius, SNT 8.7 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 7 (forecast) 8.7 Celsius, SNT 8.7 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 8 (forecast) 9.1 Celsius, SNT 8.8 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Monday and none expected on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
